Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:51:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] Explain infra: the billing-anomaly filter matches lines
 as Lambda stores them (306 fix d)

explain.yaml sets LogFormat: JSON, and src/log.ts writes each line with
console.log(string), so Lambda stores it as the string value of
"message" in {timestamp, level, requestId, message}. The filter's
top-level selectors ($.overrun, $.pausePersisted, ...) could never match,
the BillingAnomaly metric stayed 0, and the README's "the alarm makes
that failure observable" was false.

- FilterPattern is now the terms ?overrun ?billedBoundViolated
  ?pausePersisted ?E_SETTLE. src/log.ts writes those flags only when set
  and E_SETTLE is only a code, so they appear only in anomaly lines; a
  term matches the line bare, inside the JSON envelope or after the Text
  prefix. Log lines are unchanged: numeric, fixed shape, no visitor text.
- infra/aws/README.md says what is checked offline and that real alarm
  operation is unproven until the AWS sitting.

Regressions: test/billing-filter.test.ts reads the template's pattern
and runs the handler's real lines for a bound breach, an E_SETTLE whose
pause didn't persist and unknown usage, in the JSON envelope and Text
form (an answer and an ordinary refusal must not match); fails with the
old pattern. infra/aws/test_templates.py pins the pattern and checks
fixture lines in each stored form; fails with the old pattern.
Infra: 103 passed, 1 skipped (ShellCheck); cfn-lint clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
